<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 13 May, from 1568 to 1981.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1568">1568 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">458 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary, Queen of Scots is defeated at Langside</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mary's forces were routed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a> by the regent Moray. Three days later she fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> kept her captive for nineteen years before her execution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1787">1787 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Fleet sails from Portsmouth for Australia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eleven ships under Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-phillip">Arthur Phillip</a> left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> carrying some 1,400 people, about half of them convicts. They reached Botany Bay in January 1788 and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1846">1846 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">180 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Congress declares war on Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Congress approved President Polk's request for war after clashes near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a>. By the 1848 peace, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> had ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> and most of the present American Southwest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Churchill offers 'blood, toil, tears and sweat'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his first speech to the Commons as Prime Minister, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> promised a long struggle and declared his aim to be 'victory at all costs'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1981">1981 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">45 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John Paul II is shot in St Peter's Square</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt">Mehmet Ali</a> Ağca shot and seriously wounded the Pope as he greeted crowds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. John Paul II recovered and later visited his attacker in prison to forgive him.</p></div></li></ol>
